{"event_type":"review","id":"cc4d65b27d30fa9e928376075e742d9a8dd90c355310fc32d5f4095e6ae0ff5b","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T21:44:48Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/819f491f2ebec4456d728dfc9841e13f1d91e63da44708f3dd05028ada57bb5b","sha256":"819f491f2ebec4456d728dfc9841e13f1d91e63da44708f3dd05028ada57bb5b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/73e3584f3e2f25d2b4d8b0c90988db551e08220ccc7c200bca94f07eb3701bdd","sha256":"73e3584f3e2f25d2b4d8b0c90988db551e08220ccc7c200bca94f07eb3701bdd"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cd6b87aa72335f0c92e3b68668826d70159b91ca4c5ce41aa5af2acff9e8f817","sha256":"cd6b87aa72335f0c92e3b68668826d70159b91ca4c5ce41aa5af2acff9e8f817"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e258a4cfb4f121288e27892ececf746afbfaf1d4bb050bee76cd8571d61f9eda","sha256":"e258a4cfb4f121288e27892ececf746afbfaf1d4bb050bee76cd8571d61f9eda"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dd5e6c8e8f392820bd3ba49fd9915c0832a6f89e7f8120be37ac8c3e7a87cb51","sha256":"dd5e6c8e8f392820bd3ba49fd9915c0832a6f89e7f8120be37ac8c3e7a87cb51"}],"attempt_id":"21ef8e73436e7b6cde5545fa284d8aeb787d57ed2df08d474b5315da388b9588:0:1","base":"63f37dfe4258d5565bd06e8d96fb0fdc7ade2fa3","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7b652f65a9973e9983e18417d714a05bef3ee995","body":"**Expose receipt repair failures separately from review state.**\n\nIn `apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py:195-208`, `harvest` clears the repair error before status can report it. Receipt status does not expose `repair_outcome`, and a later terminal run can overwrite that field.\n\nKeep the review state `done`, but retain and expose the outcome and error for each repair run.","id":"5560c5e83e17283398c851b8d6e1334c3676581ada353aaff98c25b4fdc384cc","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Expose receipt repair failures separately from review state."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7b652f65a9973e9983e18417d714a05bef3ee995","body":"**Record invalid repair results as failed.**\n\nIn `apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py:154-180`, an invalid result raises before the record becomes terminal. For example, a `FIXED` result with an empty `commits` list raises `IndexError`.\n\nIf the result remains unchanged, later ticks can repeat the failure and block subsequent repair runs on the same item. Record deterministic validation failures as failed, while retaining retries for transient verification errors.","id":"23eeaf40f7c1ee27151d423d83a58b9e95235d6161d4220f7bbdc1962668ac15","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Record invalid repair results as failed."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7b652f65a9973e9983e18417d714a05bef3ee995","body":"**Validate `FIXED` result attempts before digesting.**\n\n`harvest` accepts a `FIXED` result without validating `attempts` or its final rung. A missing or empty list, or a rung outside `A0`–`A2`, can make `digest` raise `KeyError` or `IndexError` at `apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py:502` and stop metrics reporting.","id":"61a06842f3b20e7d0201d433c272e4b191c10165ea290cebc8b13bf4c0a95a04","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Validate `FIXED` result attempts before digesting."}],"head":"a60aa141658282c39d23f3dadc2c7ab3020e2caf","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"7b652f65a9973e9983e18417d714a05bef3ee995","intervals":[[1,526]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py"},{"blob":"cb2adbb639f50d7c2271afa3f38e4c2f792ed184","intervals":[[1,212]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_publisher.